SUMMARY:Junior Inventors - 3D Shapes
DESCRIPTION:Join us for after-school STEM programming. Open to K-8th grade families. \nTheme: Technology \nExplore the world of 3D shapes by using 3D pens\, building geometric structures out of marshmallows and toothpicks\, and forming fun towers out of Magnatiles! \nJr. Inventor program runs 4:30-6:30 PM | Museum Extended Hours! The museum will be open until 7 pm. \nFree with Admission or Membership. \n 
URL:https://owlshead.org/event/junior-inventors-3d-shapes/
LOCATION:Science & Industry Center at the Owls Head Transportation Museum\, 117 Museum St.\, Owls Head\, ME\, 04854\, United States
CATEGORIES:Summer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://owlshead.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/7.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Education":MAILTO:education@ohtm.org
END:VEVENT
