SUMMARY:STEM Saturday: Turkey STEM Day
DESCRIPTION:It’s going to be a turkey extravaganza at OHTM! Learn about aerodynamics\, kinetic energy\, and be an engineer all while creating your own feathered friends. Make a flying turkey (paper airplane or kite)\, build a house for a turkey (marshmallow/toothpick structures)\, and have a turkey balloon race (balloon rockets). \nAll-day activities for families K-8th grade. \nFree with museum admission or membership.
URL:https://owlshead.org/event/stem-saturday-turkey-stem-day/
LOCATION:Science & Industry Center at the Owls Head Transportation Museum\, 117 Museum St.\, Owls Head\, ME\, 04854\, United States
CATEGORIES:Spring
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://owlshead.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/8.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Education":MAILTO:education@ohtm.org
END:VEVENT
